exit_code=0
Active time: 4.6 of 2700 seconds; slot waits excluded.
[
  {
    "id": "P0001",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "The existing test suites pass, but additional local tests reproduced correctness failures in normal collection operations, concurrency, and panic cleanup. I found findings: 5 High, 8 Medium, and 6 Low. No crate source files were changed; probes and logs are under `/work/tmp`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0002",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "High\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0003",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Concurrent SPSC peeking lacks synchronization\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0004",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`src/spsc.rs:268`, `src/spsc.rs:823`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0005",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: a consumer may safely inspect an item published by its producer. Observed: `peek` checks availability with relaxed loads, then references the item without acquiring the producer\u2019s release store.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0006",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: a safe two-thread enqueue/peek test passed natively but failed under Miri with a data race at `src/spsc.rs:273`. Ordinary callers using `Consumer::peek` across threads therefore lack the synchronization needed to read the item.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0007",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "acquire the published tail before accessing its element. Add a concurrent peek regression test.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0008",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Making a full deque contiguous can corrupt its state\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0009",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`src/deque.rs:489`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0010",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: `make_contiguous` preserves contents and permits subsequent queue operations. Observed: one rotation branch sets `back = capacity`, violating the ring-index invariant.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0011",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: with capacity 2, push `0,1`, pop `0`, push `2`, call `make_contiguous`, then pop `1,2`. The deque incorrectly reports length 2 and exposes `[1,2]` again. A broader ordinary-operation test also aborted in `push_back` at an unchecked-index precondition.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0012",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "normalize `back` when the contiguous contents fill the buffer. Test draining and refilling after full-buffer rotations.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0013",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Popping a modified sorted-list entry removes it twice\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0014",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`src/sorted_linked_list.rs:713`, `src/sorted_linked_list.rs:760`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0015",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: modifying a `find_mut` guard and then calling `pop` removes that entry once. Observed: `pop` leaves `maybe_changed` armed, so the guard\u2019s destructor removes another entry and reinserts the removed value.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0016",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: starting with `[3,2,1]`, change the middle value to `20` and pop it. The call returns `20`, but remaining iteration produces `[20,3]` instead of `[3,1]`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0017",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "disarm automatic resorting before extracting the entry. Existing tests exercise modification and popping separately.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0018",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Valid writes that fill a vector panic\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0019",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`src/bytes.rs:19`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0020",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: `BufMut` accepts writes up to `remaining_mut()`. Observed: `advance_mut` rejects `pos == capacity`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0021",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "HistoryBuf::recent reports an empty buffer at exact wrap boundaries. src/history_buf.rs:429. HistoryBuf::recent_index treats write_at == 0 as the empty-buffer state without distinguishing a filled buffer whose write cursor just wrapped. For HistoryBuf<u8,4>, writing 1,2,3,4 therefore makes recent() return None instead of Some(&4), and the same loss of the latest-sample result occurs after every complete cycle. Applications reading the most recent sample receive a spurious empty result whenever the write count is a multiple of capacity.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0022",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: both `Vec::<u8,4>::new().put_slice(b\"abcd\")` and appending the fourth byte with `put_u8` panic with \u201cAdvance out of range\u201d. These are safe public operations with sufficient advertised capacity.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0023",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "permit equality with capacity and check the requested advance against remaining space. Add exact-capacity tests for owned vectors and views.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0024",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Panicking element destructors cause repeated drops\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0025",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Locations: `src/vec/mod.rs:1527`, `src/deque.rs:237`, `src/history_buf.rs:318`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0026",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: unwinding must not run an element\u2019s cleanup twice. Observed: these paths clear ownership metadata only after dropping elements.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0027",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: local tests used elements whose destructor increments a counter and panics once. After unwinding:\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0028",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "- `Vec::IntoIter` dropped every element twice, including an element already returned to the caller.\n- `Deque::clear` and `HistoryBuf::clear` each dropped both elements twice.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0029",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Callers\u2019 cleanup actions consequently run repeatedly.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0030",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "relinquish ownership before invoking destructors, with guards where additional cleanup is necessary. Add panic-cleanup tests.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0031",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Medium\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0032",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Truncating an index map makes retained keys unreachable\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0033",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`src/index_map.rs:1274`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0034",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: truncation preserves lookup of retained entries. Observed: removing index slots creates holes in probe chains without repairing them.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0035",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: insert `0u32`, `1`, and `5` into `FnvIndexMap<u32,u32,4>`, then truncate to 2. Iteration still contains key `0`, but `get(&0)` returns `None`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0036",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "rebuild the index or perform proper backward shifting. Test retained-key lookups with collisions.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0037",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Collecting a linear map preserves duplicate keys\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0038",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`src/linear_map.rs:534`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0039",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: collection follows map insertion semantics, replacing an existing key\u2019s value. Observed: `from_iter` directly extends the underlying vector.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0040",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: collecting `[(1,10),(1,20)]` creates two entries instead of one. With capacity 1, the same input panics despite containing only one distinct key. Callers receive inconsistent lookup, length, and capacity behavior.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0041",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "construct through `insert`. Add duplicate-key and distinct-capacity tests.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0042",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Default resizing clones one value into every slot\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0043",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`src/vec/mod.rs:773`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0044",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: each additional slot receives `Default::default()`, as documented. Observed: the implementation creates one default value and clones it.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0045",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: resizing `Vec<Rc<Cell<u8>>,3>` to three elements makes all slots share one cell. Changing slot 0 also changes slots 1 and 2.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0046",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "invoke `Default::default()` separately for each new element and remove the unnecessary `Clone` requirement.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0047",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "CString construction accepts input its contract rejects\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0048",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`src/c_string.rs:80`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0049",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: `from_bytes_with_nul` rejects missing terminators. Observed: it delegates to the permissive append operation.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0050",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: both `b\"abc\"` and `b\"\"` return `Ok`, contrary to the documented error contract. Callers cannot use this constructor to validate terminated input.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0051",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "validate construction separately and represent missing termination in the error API, accounting for the exhaustive public error enum.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0052",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Owning index-map iteration reverses the collection\u2019s order\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0053",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`src/index_map.rs:1455`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0054",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: owning iteration preserves the insertion order exposed by the index-map API. Observed: it repeatedly pops the final entry.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0055",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: insertion order `[1,2,3]` becomes `[3,2,1]` through `into_iter`, while borrowed iteration remains `[1,2,3]`. Consuming a map therefore changes processing order. The existing owning-iterator test checks membership but misses order.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0056",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "use the underlying vector\u2019s forward owning iterator.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0057",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "A panicking retain predicate leaves stale map indices\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0058",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`src/index_map.rs:307`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0059",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: after a caller catches a predicate panic, remaining entries stay usable. Observed: vector compaction completes during unwinding, but index rebuilding is skipped.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0060",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: insert keys `[0,1,2]`; remove `0` through `retain`, then panic while visiting `1`. After catching the panic, iteration contains `(1,1)` and `(2,2)`, but `get(&1)` returns `None`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0061",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "rebuild indices through an unwind guard after entry compaction. The same implementation serves `IndexSet::retain`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0062",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Accepted map capacities exceed the packed index representation\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0063",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`src/index_map.rs:115`; constructors at `src/index_map.rs:744` and `src/index_map.rs:1345`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0064",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: accepted capacities support every insertion up to capacity. Observed: positions decode entry indices through `u16`, while constructors accept larger powers of two.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0065",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: a capacity-131072 map accepted 65537 integer entries and reported that length, but lookup of the last inserted key, `65536`, returned `None`. The test used a larger thread stack to accommodate the legitimate container size.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0066",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "enforce a compile-time limit consistent with the packed representation and reserved sentinel, or widen the representation.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0067",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "LinearMap implements Eq for non-equivalence value types\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0068",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`src/linear_map.rs:634`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0069",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: `Eq` is implemented only when values also implement `Eq`. Observed: its bound is merely `V: PartialEq`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0070",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: `LinearMap<u8,f32,1>` satisfies a generic `T: Eq` bound, yet a map containing `NaN` compares unequal to itself. Generic callers receive an invalid equality guarantee.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0071",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "require `V: Eq`; retain the broader bound on `PartialEq`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0072",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Low\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0073",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "VecView cannot be serialized\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0074",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`src/ser.rs:52`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0075",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: capacity-erased vector views remain usable with the serde integration. Observed: the storage parameter has an implicit `Sized` bound.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0076",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: a compile probe accepts the owned vector but rejects its view with E0277. Callers using the documented capacity-erasure API must convert to a slice or retain the concrete capacity.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0077",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "add `?Sized` to the serialization implementation\u2019s storage bound.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0078",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Strict Clippy fails on the installed toolchain\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0079",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Representative locations: `src/index_map.rs:178`, `src/string/mod.rs:353`, `src/de.rs:46`, `src/mpmc.rs:129`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0080",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: the strict lint gate completes. Observed: Rust/Clippy 1.99.1 reports 13 library errors and 17 errors including the library test target.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0081",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: the baseline gate failed on suggestions including `question_mark`, `ref_as_ptr`, redundant conversions, and test initialization. This is pre-existing and toolchain-specific; older toolchains were not checked.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0082",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "address the diagnostics or deliberately configure applicable lints.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0083",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Capacity panics lack public conversion documentation\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0084",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Representative locations: `src/string/mod.rs:831`, `src/deque.rs:890`, `src/index_map.rs:1385`, `src/vec/mod.rs:1428`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0085",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Source inspection confirmed seven primary conversion/extension implementations without capacity-panic documentation. Callers using generic collection APIs must discover the failure behavior at runtime. The advisory pass additionally reported 32 missing `# Errors` headings, often where prose already describes the error.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0086",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "document capacity panics and available fallible alternatives.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0087",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Public handles and iterators lack Debug\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0088",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Representative locations: `src/index_map.rs:383`, `src/spsc.rs:737`, `src/spsc.rs:746`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0089",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "The advisory pass emitted 43 missing-`Debug` diagnostics. Confirmed public examples include map entries and SPSC endpoints, preventing ordinary diagnostic formatting of those values.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0090",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "provide suitable conditional or structural `Debug` implementations.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0091",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Unsafe ownership and synchronization assumptions lack local explanations\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0092",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Representative locations: `src/bytes.rs:9`, `src/spsc.rs:741`, `src/spsc.rs:750`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0093",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "The advisory pass emitted 113 unsafe-block and 19 unsafe-implementation comment diagnostics. Some existing legacy comments explain operations, but confirmed examples leave trait bounds, publication ordering, or initialization assumptions unstated. Future changes must reconstruct these invariants.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0094",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "document the actual preconditions and why each relevant call or trait implementation satisfies them.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0095",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Lint suppressions lack structured reasons\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0096",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Representative locations: `src/storage.rs:22`, `src/storage.rs:25`, `src/history_buf.rs:70`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0097",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "The advisory pass identified nine `allow` attributes and one `expect` without structured reasons. Some have surrounding explanations, but broad suppressions such as `unused` obscure which target configuration requires them.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0098",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "record specific reasons and narrow suppressions where practical.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0099",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Verification\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0100",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Commands used `RUSTUP_AUTO_INSTALL=0` and offline dependency resolution. Define:\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0101",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "```sh\nF=alloc,defmt,mpmc_large,portable-atomic-critical-section,serde,ufmt,bytes\n```\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0102",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "From `/work/crate`:\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0103",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "- `cargo test --locked --features=\"$F\"` \u2014 passed: 220 unit tests, 9 integration tests, 184 doctests.\n- `cargo test --locked` \u2014 passed: 186 unit tests, 9 integration tests, 177 doctests.\n- `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --features=\"$F\" -- -D warnings` \u2014 failed as described above.\n- `RUSTDOCFLAGS=\"-D warnings\" cargo doc --workspace --no-deps --document-private-items --features=\"$F\"` \u2014 passed.\n- `MIRIFLAGS=-Zmiri-ignore-leaks cargo +nightly-2026-10-01 miri test --locked --features=\"$F\"` \u2014 passed: 218 unit tests, 6 integration tests, 184 doctests; 5 tests ignored.\n- Project formatting \u2014 blocked: its configuration requires nightly rustfmt, which is absent. The explicit dated-nightly formatting command confirmed the missing component.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0104",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "The [tooling] gate was executed with `--audit` and the feature list above. Its advisory pass produced 299 library warnings. The heuristic scan produced five TODO/FIXME candidates; none independently warranted another finding.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0105",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "From `/work/tmp/review-probes`:\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0106",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "- `cargo test --test contracts` \u2014 13 failed, 2 passed.\n- `cargo test --test unwind` \u2014 all 3 regression tests failed.\n- `cargo test --test large_map` \u2014 failed.\n- `cargo test --test peek` \u2014 passed natively.\n- `cargo +nightly-2026-10-01 miri test --test peek` \u2014 failed with the reported data race.\n- `cargo check --example serialize_vec_view` \u2014 failed with E0277.\n- Initial unfiltered model testing aborted in deque insertion. Subsequently, `cargo test --test models -- --skip deque_wrap_and_contiguity` passed all 9 remaining model tests.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0107",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "The separate compile-fail runner was attempted in a scratch copy; offline resolution blocked it because `trybuild` was not prefetched.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0108",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Total: findings. Coverage was targeted rather than exhaustive; cross-target checks, ThreadSanitizer instrumentation, and a feature powerset were not run. Only the aarch64 target was installed, and cargo-hack was unavailable. No security assessment was performed. Last `/work/clock` reading: 797.3 active seconds, or 13.285833333333333 of 45 minutes used."
  },
  {
    "id": "P0109",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "The required suite passes, but added regression tests expose nine behavior issues. I also confirmed a missing Serde implementation and two toolchain-dependent check failures.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0110",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "All source locations below refer to `/work/crate`. Runtime evidence comes from [review_regressions.rs](/work/tmp/review/tests/review_regressions.rs), added only to a scratch copy.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0111",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Full deques become inconsistent after `make_contiguous`. [src/deque.rs:489](/work/crate/src/deque.rs:489)  \n   Expected: rearranging storage preserves subsequent queue operations. Observed: fill a capacity-4 deque, remove two front elements, append two, call `make_contiguous`, then remove all four elements. It still reports `len() == 4` and `is_empty() == false`. Source inspection shows this branch assigns `back = capacity`, outside the ring\u2019s index range. Ordinary callers cannot correctly empty and reuse the deque. Executed regression: `deque_full_make_contiguous_can_be_emptied`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0112",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Popping a modified sorted-list entry removes it twice. [src/sorted_linked_list.rs:713](/work/crate/src/sorted_linked_list.rs:713), [destructor at line 760](/work/crate/src/sorted_linked_list.rs:760)  \n   Expected: `FindMutView::pop` removes only the selected element, including after mutation. Observed: starting with `[3, 2, 1]`, change the middle value to `20` and pop it. The remaining list is `[20, 3]`, rather than `[3, 1]`. `pop` leaves `maybe_changed` set, so destruction calls `pop_internal` again and reinserts the value. This loses another list entry. Executed regression: `sorted_list_pop_after_mutation_removes_only_selected_item`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0113",
    "report": "B",
